## DONE vs REMAINING

**Tree:** `wave7-design` · branch `design/ledgerline-ui` · commit `b8ae695` (not pushed — you review and merge).

### First: the five components were already built

They landed in `2da2189` before this turn. I verified rather than rebuilt: all five exist, `SemicircularGauge` matches the critique's literal spec (viewBox `0 0 200 110`, r=80, stroke 18, `stroke-linecap="butt"`, flat baseline cuts), and `des-check`/lint/30 tests/build were green. Rebuilding them would have been churn.

### What I found by re-reading instead of trusting the record

The prior report said *"every scaffold string in the gallery (api-gateway, eu-west, v2.4.1) is gone."* **It was not.** `FloatingSurfaceDemo.tsx` had never been touched and still carried all three. A claim the diff can't support is worse than no claim, so this pass re-read the tree:

- **Rule 8 fiction** — `FloatingSurfaceDemo` now uses `INV-2026-07-0142` / `Northwind Robotics` / a dunning-retry count; `components-view`'s `1.2M requests / 184ms P95` (cloud telemetry in a billing product) became collected-this-period and collection rate; `home-view`'s `NS One` theme and hardcoded `Routes='6'` naming deleted routes are now `Ledgerline` and a derived count; `_app.tsx` no longer calls Ledgerline a "starter scaffold". `NS One` → `Ledgerline` across the design views.
- **`dashboard-view.tsx` deleted** — 165 lines, **zero importers**, carrying a fabricated `612ms`.
- **A 404 shipped** — `home-view` linked `/dashboard`, but `routes/dashboard.tsx` was deleted with the scaffold routes.

### Ranked item 2 was only half done

`DeltaChip` existed, but `StatsGrid` still parked it in the header beside the label — the exact placement the critic refused (`stats-grid.tsx` was untouched by `2da2189`). Added a `delta` slot that rides on the value's own row; `badge` stays for the header, so existing call sites are unaffected.

### On the test I nearly shipped broken

My first dead-link test **matched zero hrefs** — every `href` in `home-view` is a JSX expression — so it passed while proving nothing. I caught it, rewrote it to scan the whole app, and verified by reintroducing `/dashboard` and watching it fail. It now also asserts it checked something, so future refactors can't make it quietly vacuous. Both new rules (`R8`) follow your pattern of making each fix un-regressable — which is what caught this class of overclaim in the first place.

Verified: `deno check` 0 errors, lint clean, fmt clean, **30 tests pass**, `vite build` succeeds, **`deno.lock` untouched**.

### REMAINING — one thing I deliberately did not do

**The `wave7-billing` handoff is blocked, and I stopped rather than force it.** Four opencode agents are live in that tree right now (commits seconds apart), and one is mid-refactor on the *exact* files this task names — steer #9 is rewriting `MoneyText` and moving `ns-exception-badge` rules into `assets/ui/*.css`. There's also a recorded incident in this repo of edits being "swept into a shared commit by accident." Editing there would have collided or been silently absorbed.

Still unfixed there, exactly as reported: `money-text.tsx` (`Number(text)` → `$100` not `$100.00`; `100.00USD` with no separator), `exception-badge.css:7-9` (`--ns-rust-6` at 45.5% L on a 21.5% dark card), plus the offset shadows in `button.css`, `desktop-update-prompt.css`, and the `paper-12` leaks in `sheet.css`/`switch.css`. All are already fixed on this branch and apply unchanged once those agents settle.

**One design gap worth your call:** `DeltaChip` colours purely by `direction`, so it has no "a decrease is good" tone — *failed payments −3.1%* renders red, which is a false statement in the same family as `0.00` for "not measured". I picked metrics where direction maps honestly rather than ship a lying colour, but this needs a real fix for a billing product.
